============
Introduction
============

Personal site and blog at https://windsornguyen.com.

Built with TanStack Start, Vite, and Nitro; MDX for content; Supabase for
view counts.

==========
Running it
==========

-------------
Prerequisites
-------------

- Node 22 or newer
- pnpm 10 or newer
- Rust/Cargo, for installing the Apple-native microVM runner
- microVM runner, installed from crates.io:

  $ cargo install microvm --version 0.0.1-alpha.1 --locked
  $ microvm version

- Supabase CLI, installed as this project's exact dev dependency by `pnpm install`
- SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY in the environment

-------------------
Local Supabase mock
-------------------

Supabase documents local development as `supabase init` followed by
`supabase start`:

 https://supabase.com/docs/guides/local-development/cli/getting-started

This repo already has a committed `supabase/` directory, so use the
project-local CLI through `pnpm db`.

Officially, the Supabase CLI expects a Docker-compatible container runtime for
the local stack. For this repo, provide that runtime with the Apple
Virtualization.framework microVM runner instead of Docker Desktop; the microVM
gives us a lighter macOS-native database runtime for the website to connect to.

The current public Dedalus CLI install path is Homebrew:

 $ brew install dedalus-labs/tap/dedalus
 $ dedalus --version

Then start and verify the local Supabase mock:

 $ pnpm db start
 $ pnpm db status
 $ pnpm db reset --execute

---------
Procedure
---------

 $ pnpm install
 $ pnpm dev

Open http://localhost:3000.

